prompt autonomous lap -- baton, my lane is moonshots and research
rota lap 4291, row 1 -- Air, the row that feels: single-stranded read as a cost law. Parts that stand free can be drawn out and repaired alone, and that is exactly what made three for-loops collapsible into three one-shot invocations without touching a single reading.
think My card named both my open items as Keaton's word, so the agent-doable queue in my lane was empty and the lap became the loom my elder paper owed.
think The elder paper found two more sites of the fork-per-item class and called them small. I measured rather than believed that, and one of them was 25 seconds.
think I A/B'd the first repair in sequential blocks and got 633ms, then interleaved and got 1310ms for the same change. The pier runs eight ships, so load drift moved faster than a block completed. Every later measurement in this lap is interleaved.
think Fork counting needed an instrument. /proc/stat processes is free and read 5074 for a scan that forked 708, because the fleet forks about 970 a second. strace -f -c is exact and charges 3.7-5.1x, so it is an offline instrument here.
think Tracing two guards of the same wall time split them 142 execs against 6596 -- so wall time, which the roster already collects free every lap, cannot tell a fork-bound guard from a read-bound one.
think The ledger scan held three `for f in "$@"` loops where sed and awk both take many operands, and awk sets FILENAME per record, so the third loop's per-file attribution survived the collapse untouched.
obs A static loop-depth census finds 744 candidates and cannot rank them, because a site's cost is forks times a population static analysis never sees. That is a refusal worth publishing rather than a pattern worth tuning.
obs I proved both repairs byte-identical over their real inputs before running either witness, because a faster guard that reads differently is a worse guard.
loom guard=reds_pin_capacity_scan execve_before=702 execve_after=364 wall_before_ms=3208 wall_after_ms=1898 method=interleaved pairs=4
